Hi Josue,

I can see some issues:
Some of the variograms look like the individual isn't resident during the tracking period. The biggest red flags are PS0026_ASI13 and PS0005_ASI12.
Individual PS0095_ASI12 (and maybe some others) doesn't appear to be moving much at all, and would need a location error model to better resolve (but this is probably just nesting behavior or something?).
Between the largest migratory/dispersal ranges and the smallest nest-bound ranges, there's 6 orders of magnitude difference in range area, so the default grid (largest extent at highest resolution) probably won't work. So even if the data didn't need any cleaning, you would want to specify a coarser resolution or change the resolution calculation (see the help('akde') grid arguments).
Best,
Chris

