Hi Chris,

First, I'd like to estimate the % of time spent within a polygon, so as recommended in a previous post, I extracted the PMF from each individual's OD and summed the values within the polygon. To get an average time spent within the polygon across all animals, I took the weighted mean of the summed PMF, where the weights were the track length in days used to estimate the OD. Does that sound about right?

Second, I'd like provide a visual/spatial summary of where most activity occurred during the monitoring period. Instead of displaying all individual ODs on one map, I was wondering if there's any way to summarize the information from all the ODs in any meaningful way. I'd like to have one layer that indicates the "hot spots" of documented activity - or as Dani previously described "a composite raster layer for each season that represents something like population-level intensity of use for any given pixel". I was wondering if there was any good way to do this when both the sampling period and frequency differs.

Best,
Christina

